# Entitlements & Billing Separation

**Billing** owns subscription lifecycle and all direct integration with a payment
provider (e.g. Stripe): webhooks, invoices, payment methods.

**Entitlements** owns the answer to "what can this tenant do/use right now?" —
plan limits, feature flags, seat counts — derived *from* subscription state, but
without talking to the payment provider itself.

## Why they're separate modules

- Feature-check code (called frequently, on hot paths across the app) must never
  depend on payment-provider SDKs, network calls, or webhook-processing logic.
- Payment-provider outages/changes should never be able to break unrelated
  feature-flag checks.
- This keeps Billing's provider-specific concerns (webhooks, retries, PCI-adjacent
  concerns) isolated from the rest of the system.

## Rule

`PTS.Modules.Entitlements` must not reference `PTS.Modules.Billing` directly (or
vice versa). When Billing needs to communicate a subscription-state change that
affects entitlements, do it through a contract in `PTS.SharedKernel` or
composition in `PTS.Host` — not a direct project reference. This is also enforced
by the general module-boundary rule in `00-modular-monolith-architecture.mdc`.

## Phase 1 status

Both modules are currently empty scaffolding. Do not implement subscriptions,
Stripe integration, or entitlement checks until a later phase explicitly asks for
it.
